{
  "statement": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real Hilbert Borel space with canonical volume, including the explicit rank-zero extension. Let V:E→ℝ be C², 0<α≤β, and assume α‖v‖²≤D²V(x)[v,v]≤β‖v‖² for every x,v. Assume η>0 and βη≤1. Define μ(dx) proportional to exp(−V(x))dx, J as the law of (X,X+√η Z) for independent X~μ and Z~N(0,I), ν=J.snd, and Λ as the law of (Y,2X−Y) under J. These are probability laws. Put mY=comap(snd), H_P=L² classes measurable with respect to mY, P=i∘E[·|Y] and the canonical M:u↦u∘snd. Then H_P=ran(P), P is identity on H_P, and there exists an onto linear isometry e:L²(ν;ℝ)≃H_P with i e=M. There is a Markov kernel S whose every-state normalized law is S(y)=volume.tilted(x↦−V((y+x)/2)−‖y−x‖²/(8η)); Λ.IsCondKernel S and both Λ marginals equal ν. The same joint reflection F(x,y)=(x,2x−y) gives the involutive selfadjoint isometry U, with Uf=f∘F J-almost everywhere for every f. There is a bounded selfadjoint T on the full real L²(ν), with ‖Tu‖≤‖u‖, Tu(y)=∫u(x)S(y,dx) ν-almost everywhere for each u, and preserved integral. On H_P put A=PUP restricted via i and orthogonal projection, and B=(I_J−P)UPi:H_P→L²(J). Then A=eTe⁻¹ is selfadjoint and contractive, PB=0. There is a bounded positive real scalar Γ with Γ²=I−T². For the SAME transported Γ_P=eΓe⁻¹, positivity holds and Γ_P²=I_H_P−A²=B*B. Every f∈H_P satisfies ‖Bf‖=‖Γ_Pf‖ and ‖Γ_Pf‖²=‖f‖²−‖Af‖². EVERY bounded positive G on H_P whose square is I_H_P−A² equals Γ_P, independently of any energy premise. The genuine original-input consumer additionally derives ‖Γ_Pf‖≤‖f‖. Closedness/completeness, normalization, onto-M, positivity, roots and energy are internally derived; no caller certificate is assumed.",
  "paper_assumptions": "Original C² finite real Hilbert/Borel potential, 0<α≤β, both global Hessians, η>0, βη≤1. Rank-zero base extension and legal αη=1 remain explicit; L² is not assumed finite-dimensional.",
  "route_boundary": "Selected printed B1-B5 first Gram identity/B10-B11 on the exact closed macro domain H_P=lpMeas=ran(P), using the SAME actual M/e/U/T and transported root. Full-joint Gram is P−A_J², not I_J−A_J². The other B5 identity, centered root order/inverse/polar, H1, event process/nonexplosion/invariance/hypocoercivity/main mixing, implementation error and actual-input expected query costs/composition remain separate.",
  "units": [
    {
      "title": "Actual PBPS: the unique positive macroscopic defect root",
      "steps": [
        {
          "title": "Produce the actual probability laws and reflected conditional operator",
          "text": "Under the original C², both global Hessian bounds and capped positive η, the accepted actual centered-defect producer gives probability μ,J,ν, the every-y normalized reflected S, stationary disintegration, literal reflection U and selfadjoint contractive mean-preserving scalar T. Align independently produced pullbacks/reflections by their every-observable almost-everywhere action; no alternate kernel or operator is supplied.",
          "formula": "\\Lambda\\in\\mathrm{CondKernel}(S),\\quad\\Lambda_1=\\Lambda_2=\\nu,\\quad Uf=f\\circ F\\ (J\\text{-a.e.}),\\quad Tu(y)=\\int u(x)S(y,dx)\\ (\\nu\\text{-a.e.}).",
          "lean": "  rcases CenteredDefectOperator.actual_centered_selfadjoint_defect hα hαβ hV hH hη hβη with\n    ⟨hμ,hJ,hν,S,hS,hSd,hSc,hSf,hSs,U,hU,hUi,hUs,M0,hM0,T,hTs,hAll,\n      q,hqa,hTq,hqi,hzero,hD,hDq,hDef,hRest⟩\n  letI : IsProbabilityMeasure μ := hμ\n  letI : IsProbabilityMeasure J := hJ\n  letI : IsProbabilityMeasure ν := hν\n  have hM0eq : M0 = M := by\n    apply LinearIsometry.ext\n    intro u\n    apply Lp.ext\n    exact (hM0 u).trans (Lp.coeFn_compMeasurePreserving u hp).symm\n  subst M0\n",
          "detail": "Exact excerpt from the compiled declaration in its local context; preceding canonical lets and earlier proved facts remain in scope.",
          "lean_source_region": {
            "path": "AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/ProximalBPS/MacroscopicDefectRoot.lean",
            "source_raw_sha256": "1022d344a428efaafd7443c65317c5bde0a2f3ed05161caaac8bf15ae239858a",
            "start_line": 91,
            "end_line": 102,
            "exact_code_raw_sha256": "14ba571b02108b891dae44626de041a84e5e69e7b1aaab13c00ad577be0d1ed3"
          }
        },
        {
          "title": "Identify the exact closed macro space and canonical onto isometry",
          "text": "The conditional projection equals the orthogonal projection onto H_P=lpMeas. Its range is H_P and it fixes every vector in H_P. The accepted actual range theorem identifies the SAME canonical M range with ran(P); restrict M to its range and use that equality to obtain the isometric equivalence e with inclusion i e=M. Ambient product measurability and completeness of the closed subspace are derived internally.",
          "formula": "H_P=\\operatorname{ran}P=\\operatorname{ran}M,\\quad P|_{H_P}=I_{H_P},\\quad e:L^2(\\nu;\\mathbb R)\\simeq H_P,\\quad ie=M.",
          "lean": "  have hPdef : P = HP.starProjection := rfl\n  have hPrange : P.toLinearMap.range = HP := by\n    change P.range = HP\n    rw [hPdef]\n    exact HP.range_starProjection\n  have hMR : M.toLinearMap.range = P.toLinearMap.range :=\n    (MacroscopicRange.actual_macroscopic_centered_range hα hαβ hV hH hη hβη).2.2.1\n  let e : Lp ℝ 2 ν ≃ₗᵢ[ℝ] HP :=\n    M.equivRange.trans (LinearIsometryEquiv.ofEq _ _ (hMR.trans hPrange))\n  have he (u : Lp ℝ 2 ν) : (e u : Lp ℝ 2 J) = M u := rfl\n  have hPf (f : HP) : P (f : Lp ℝ 2 J) = f := by\n    rw [hPdef]\n    exact HP.starProjection_mem_subspace_eq_self f\n  have hPP : P*P=P := by rw [hPdef];exact HP.isIdempotentElem_starProjection\n  have hPid (f : Lp ℝ 2 J) : P (P f)=P f := by\n    change (P*P) f=P f\n    rw [hPP]\n",
          "detail": "Exact excerpt from the compiled declaration in its local context; preceding canonical lets and earlier proved facts remain in scope.",
          "lean_source_region": {
            "path": "AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/ProximalBPS/MacroscopicDefectRoot.lean",
            "source_raw_sha256": "1022d344a428efaafd7443c65317c5bde0a2f3ed05161caaac8bf15ae239858a",
            "start_line": 103,
            "end_line": 119,
            "exact_code_raw_sha256": "09d303c9d3174b175547fd2ff6f12f057baec3bd99ac28f146f610cae26d1c66"
          }
        },
        {
          "title": "Identify the same macroscopic reflected operator",
          "text": "The already proved pullback intertwining relation evaluated at e⁻¹f yields A=eTe⁻¹. Isometric conjugation preserves selfadjointness, and norm preservation transfers the scalar contraction to every macro f. The ambient operator A_J=PUP and the macro endomorphism A are kept separately typed.",
          "formula": "A_J=PUP,\\quad iAf=A_Jif,\\quad A=eTe^{-1},\\quad A^*=A,\\quad\\|Af\\|\\le\\|f\\|.",
          "lean": "  let A : HP →L[ℝ] HP :=\n              HP.orthogonalProjectionOnto ∘L U.toContinuousLinearMap ∘L HP.subtypeL\n            let B : HP →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 J :=\n              (((1 : Lp ℝ 2 J →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 J)-P)*U.toContinuousLinearMap*P) ∘L HP.subtypeL\n            A = e.conjStarAlgEquiv T ∧ IsSelfAdjoint A ∧\n            (∀ f : HP, ‖A f‖ ≤ ‖f‖) ∧\n            (∀ f : HP, P (B f) = 0) ∧\n            ∃ Γ : Lp ℝ 2 ν →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 ν,\n              Γ.IsPositive ∧ Γ*Γ=(1 : Lp ℝ 2 ν →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 ν)-T*T ∧\n              let ΓP : HP →L[ℝ] HP := e.conjStarAlgEquiv Γ\n              ΓP.IsPositive ∧ ΓP*ΓP=(1 : HP →L[ℝ] HP)-A*A ∧\n              B.adjoint ∘L B = ΓP*ΓP ∧\n              (∀ f : HP, ‖B f‖ = ‖ΓP f‖ ∧\n                ‖ΓP f‖^2 = ‖f‖^2-‖A f‖^2) ∧\n              (∀ G : HP →L[ℝ] HP,\n                G.IsPositive → G*G=(1 : HP →L[ℝ] HP)-A*A → G=ΓP)\n:= by\n  classical\n  dsimp only\n  let μ := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x => -V x)\n  let J := (μ.prod (stdGaussian E)).map\n    (fun p : E × E => (p.1,p.1+Real.sqrt η • p.2))\n  let ν := J.snd\n  let mY : MeasurableSpace (E × E) := MeasurableSpace.comap Prod.snd (inferInstance : MeasurableSpace E)\n  letI : MeasurableSpace (E × E) := Prod.instMeasurableSpace\n  letI : Fact (mY ≤ (inferInstance : MeasurableSpace (E × E))) :=\n    ⟨measurable_snd.comap_le⟩\n  let HP := lpMeas ℝ ℝ mY 2 J\n  letI : NormedAddCommGroup HP := HP.normedAddCommGroup\n  letI : InnerProductSpace ℝ HP := HP.innerProductSpace\n  let P : Lp ℝ 2 J →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 J :=\n    HP.subtypeL ∘L condExpL2 ℝ ℝ (μ := J) measurable_snd.comap_le\n  let hp : MeasurePreserving (Prod.snd : E × E → E) J ν := ⟨measurable_snd,rfl⟩\n  let M : Lp ℝ 2 ν →ₗᵢ[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 J := Lp.compMeasurePreservingₗᵢ ℝ Prod.snd hp\n  rcases CenteredDefectOperator.actual_centered_selfadjoint_defect hα hαβ hV hH hη hβη with\n    ⟨hμ,hJ,hν,S,hS,hSd,hSc,hSf,hSs,U,hU,hUi,hUs,M0,hM0,T,hTs,hAll,\n      q,hqa,hTq,hqi,hzero,hD,hDq,hDef,hRest⟩\n  letI : IsProbabilityMeasure μ := hμ\n  letI : IsProbabilityMeasure J := hJ\n  letI : IsProbabilityMeasure ν := hν\n  have hM0eq : M0 = M := by\n    apply LinearIsometry.ext\n    intro u\n    apply Lp.ext\n    exact (hM0 u).trans (Lp.coeFn_compMeasurePreserving u hp).symm\n  subst M0\n  have hPdef : P = HP.starProjection := rfl\n  have hPrange : P.toLinearMap.range = HP := by\n    change P.range = HP\n    rw [hPdef]\n    exact HP.range_starProjection\n  have hMR : M.toLinearMap.range = P.toLinearMap.range :=\n    (MacroscopicRange.actual_macroscopic_centered_range hα hαβ hV hH hη hβη).2.2.1\n  let e : Lp ℝ 2 ν ≃ₗᵢ[ℝ] HP :=\n    M.equivRange.trans (LinearIsometryEquiv.ofEq _ _ (hMR.trans hPrange))\n  have he (u : Lp ℝ 2 ν) : (e u : Lp ℝ 2 J) = M u := rfl\n  have hPf (f : HP) : P (f : Lp ℝ 2 J) = f := by\n    rw [hPdef]\n    exact HP.starProjection_mem_subspace_eq_self f\n  have hPP : P*P=P := by rw [hPdef];exact HP.isIdempotentElem_starProjection\n  have hPid (f : Lp ℝ 2 J) : P (P f)=P f := by\n    change (P*P) f=P f\n    rw [hPP]\n  let A : HP →L[ℝ] HP :=\n    HP.orthogonalProjectionOnto ∘L U.toContinuousLinearMap ∘L HP.subtypeL\n  let B0 : Lp ℝ 2 J →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 J :=\n    ((1 : Lp ℝ 2 J →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 J)-P)*U.toContinuousLinearMap*P\n  let AJ := P*U.toContinuousLinearMap*P\n  let B : HP →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 J := B0 ∘L HP.subtypeL\n  have hAincl (f : HP) : (A f : Lp ℝ 2 J) = AJ f := by\n    change P (U f) = P (U (P f))\n    rw [hPf]\n  have hAeq : A=e.conjStarAlgEquiv T := by\n    apply ContinuousLinearMap.ext\n    intro f\n    apply Subtype.ext\n    change (A f : Lp ℝ 2 J) = (e (T (e.symm f)) : Lp ℝ 2 J)\n    rw [hAincl,he]\n    have hf : M (e.symm f) = (f : Lp ℝ 2 J) := by\n      rw [← he,e.apply_symm_apply]\n    rw [← hf]\n    exact ((hAll (e.symm f)).2.1).symm\n  have hAapply (f : HP) : A f=e (T (e.symm f)) := by rw [hAeq];rfl\n  have hAs : IsSelfAdjoint A := by\n    rw [hAeq]\n    simpa only [LinearIsometryEquiv.conjStarAlgEquiv_apply,e.adjoint_eq_symm] using\n      hTs.conj_adjoint (e : Lp ℝ 2 ν →L[ℝ] HP)\n  have hAn (f : HP) : ‖A f‖ ≤ ‖f‖ := by\n    rw [hAapply,e.norm_map]\n    exact ((hAll (e.symm f)).2.2.1).trans_eq (e.symm.norm_map f)\n",
          "detail": "Exact excerpt from the compiled declaration in its local context; preceding canonical lets and earlier proved facts remain in scope.",
          "lean_source_region": {
            "path": "AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/ProximalBPS/MacroscopicDefectRoot.lean",
            "source_raw_sha256": "1022d344a428efaafd7443c65317c5bde0a2f3ed05161caaac8bf15ae239858a",
            "start_line": 57,
            "end_line": 146,
            "exact_code_raw_sha256": "d4b931631b5995d6e13d7b177d06aac175dffcec137ffc204d938203759b38a0"
          }
        },
        {
          "title": "Restrict the correct full-joint Gram identity",
          "text": "Write B₀=(I_J−P)UP and B=B₀i. Projection idempotence gives PBf=0. The actual reflection block theorem gives B₀*B₀=P−A_J². Compose with i* and i; using Pi=i and iA=A_Ji, this becomes B*B=I_H_P−A². Replacing full-joint P by I_J would be false, including U=I with a nonidentity P.",
          "formula": "PB=0,\\quad B_0^*B_0=P-A_J^2,\\quad B^*B=i^*(P-A_J^2)i=I_{H_P}-A^2.",
          "lean": "  have hPB (f : HP) : P (B f)=0 := by\n    change P (U (P f)-P (U (P f)))=0\n    rw [map_sub,hPid,sub_self]\n  obtain ⟨R,hR,hRf,U2,hU2,hU2i,hU2s,hRp,hBB,hBD,hBE⟩ :=\n    ReflectionL2.actual_reflection_block_identities μ hη\n  have hU2eq : U2=U := by\n    apply LinearIsometry.ext\n    intro f\n    apply Lp.ext\n    exact (hU2 f).trans (hU f).symm\n  subst U2\n  have hB0Gram : B0.adjoint ∘L B0=P-AJ*AJ := by\n    have hBBtyped : B0.adjoint ∘L B0 = P-AJ^2 := hBB\n    simpa only [pow_two] using hBBtyped\n",
          "detail": "Exact excerpt from the compiled declaration in its local context; preceding canonical lets and earlier proved facts remain in scope.",
          "lean_source_region": {
            "path": "AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/ProximalBPS/MacroscopicDefectRoot.lean",
            "source_raw_sha256": "1022d344a428efaafd7443c65317c5bde0a2f3ed05161caaac8bf15ae239858a",
            "start_line": 147,
            "end_line": 160,
            "exact_code_raw_sha256": "afd3fdf71a730dd25db274c1c2b635124bee27e7fb4399a020f334b6eb6e34f2"
          }
        },
        {
          "title": "Transport the internally constructed positive real scalar root",
          "text": "The shared real L² root theorem produces Γ≥0 with Γ²=I−T². Define Γ_P by the SAME e-conjugation. Adjoint conjugation preserves positivity; the star-algebra equivalence preserves multiplication, subtraction and identity, so Γ_P²=I_H_P−A² and agrees with the preceding typed Gram operator. No real CFC or root witness is a public premise.",
          "formula": "\\Gamma\\ge0,\\quad\\Gamma^2=I-T^2,\\quad\\Gamma_P=e\\Gamma e^{-1}\\ge0,\\quad\\Gamma_P^2=I_{H_P}-A^2=B^*B.",
          "lean": "  obtain ⟨Γ,hΓ,hΓSq,hEnergy⟩ :=\n    AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Measure.L2RealSquareRoot.exists_positive_real_square_root\n      ν ((1 : Lp ℝ 2 ν →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 ν)-T*T) hD\n  let ΓP : HP →L[ℝ] HP := e.conjStarAlgEquiv Γ\n  have hΓP : ΓP.IsPositive := by\n    simpa only [ΓP,LinearIsometryEquiv.conjStarAlgEquiv_apply,e.adjoint_eq_symm] using\n      hΓ.conj_adjoint (e : Lp ℝ 2 ν →L[ℝ] HP)\n  have hΓPSq : ΓP*ΓP=(1 : HP →L[ℝ] HP)-A*A := by\n    change e.conjStarAlgEquiv Γ*e.conjStarAlgEquiv Γ=_\n    rw [← map_mul,hΓSq,map_sub,map_one,map_mul,← hAeq]\n  have hGram : B.adjoint ∘L B=ΓP*ΓP := by\n    calc\n      B.adjoint ∘L B = HP.subtypeL.adjoint ∘L (B0.adjoint ∘L B0) ∘L HP.subtypeL := by\n        simp only [B,ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint_comp,ContinuousLinearMap.comp_assoc]\n      _ = HP.subtypeL.adjoint ∘L (P-AJ*AJ) ∘L HP.subtypeL := by rw [hB0Gram]\n      _ = (1 : HP →L[ℝ] HP)-A*A := by\n        apply ContinuousLinearMap.ext\n        intro f\n        rw [HP.adjoint_subtypeL]\n        change HP.orthogonalProjectionOnto (P f-AJ (AJ f))=f-A (A f)\n        rw [hPf,← hAincl f,← hAincl (A f),map_sub]\n        simp only [Submodule.orthogonalProjectionOnto_mem_subspace_eq_self]\n      _ = ΓP*ΓP := hΓPSq.symm\n",
          "detail": "Exact excerpt from the compiled declaration in its local context; preceding canonical lets and earlier proved facts remain in scope.",
          "lean_source_region": {
            "path": "AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/ProximalBPS/MacroscopicDefectRoot.lean",
            "source_raw_sha256": "1022d344a428efaafd7443c65317c5bde0a2f3ed05161caaac8bf15ae239858a",
            "start_line": 161,
            "end_line": 183,
            "exact_code_raw_sha256": "7c5af75665a2b5adfe58636bcbca4de702618af770199c4e78af69f98f8c3467"
          }
        },
        {
          "title": "Recover the macro norm and energy identities",
          "text": "Apply the scalar energy theorem to e⁻¹f and use the same isometry and A-conjugation to obtain macro energy. The adjoint inner-product identities for B and the positive selfadjoint Γ_P have equal squared norms since B*B=Γ_P²; nonnegative norms then give equality of norms.",
          "formula": "\\|Bf\\|=\\|\\Gamma_Pf\\|,\\quad\\|\\Gamma_Pf\\|^2=\\|f\\|^2-\\|Af\\|^2\\quad(f\\in H_P).",
          "lean": "  have hMacroEnergy (f : HP) : ‖ΓP f‖^2=‖f‖^2-‖A f‖^2 := by\n    have hs : ‖Γ (e.symm f)‖^2=‖e.symm f‖^2-‖T (e.symm f)‖^2 :=\n      (hEnergy (e.symm f)).trans (hDef (e.symm f))\n    simpa only [ΓP,LinearIsometryEquiv.conjStarAlgEquiv_apply_apply,hAapply,\n      e.norm_map,e.symm.norm_map] using hs\n  have hNorm (f : HP) : ‖B f‖=‖ΓP f‖ := by\n    have hb := B.apply_norm_sq_eq_inner_adjoint_right f\n    have hg := ΓP.apply_norm_sq_eq_inner_adjoint_right f\n    rw [hGram] at hb\n    rw [hΓP.isSelfAdjoint.adjoint_eq] at hg\n    exact (sq_eq_sq₀ (norm_nonneg _) (norm_nonneg _)).mp (hb.trans hg.symm)\n",
          "detail": "Exact excerpt from the compiled declaration in its local context; preceding canonical lets and earlier proved facts remain in scope.",
          "lean_source_region": {
            "path": "AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/ProximalBPS/MacroscopicDefectRoot.lean",
            "source_raw_sha256": "1022d344a428efaafd7443c65317c5bde0a2f3ed05161caaac8bf15ae239858a",
            "start_line": 184,
            "end_line": 194,
            "exact_code_raw_sha256": "d0a98bb18eb0c0cffc017a43279e6807c67614afaca6feb61dcb55d8698e0198"
          }
        },
        {
          "title": "Prove uniqueness for every positive same-square macro alternative",
          "text": "For ANY positive G with G²=I_H_P−A², pull it back by e⁻¹. Its positivity and square are preserved, so the shared real scalar uniqueness theorem forces e⁻¹Ge=Γ. Conjugate back to obtain G=Γ_P. The universal alternative-root quantifier is outside the every-f energy conjunction and assumes no alternative energy identity.",
          "formula": "G\\ge0,\\ G^2=I_{H_P}-A^2\\ \\Longrightarrow\\ e^{-1}Ge=\\Gamma\\ \\Longrightarrow\\ G=\\Gamma_P.",
          "lean": "  have hUnique (G : HP →L[ℝ] HP) (hG : G.IsPositive)\n      (hGSq : G*G=(1 : HP →L[ℝ] HP)-A*A) : G=ΓP := by\n    let G0 : Lp ℝ 2 ν →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 ν := e.symm.conjStarAlgEquiv G\n    have hG0 : G0.IsPositive := by\n      simpa only [G0,LinearIsometryEquiv.conjStarAlgEquiv_apply,e.symm.adjoint_eq_symm] using\n        hG.conj_adjoint (e.symm : HP →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 ν)\n    have hPullA : e.symm.conjStarAlgEquiv A=T := by\n      rw [hAeq]\n      apply ContinuousLinearMap.ext\n      intro u\n      simp only [LinearIsometryEquiv.conjStarAlgEquiv_apply_apply,\n        LinearIsometryEquiv.symm_symm,e.symm_apply_apply,e.apply_symm_apply]\n    have hG0Sq : G0*G0=(1 : Lp ℝ 2 ν →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 ν)-T*T := by\n      change e.symm.conjStarAlgEquiv G*e.symm.conjStarAlgEquiv G=_\n      rw [← map_mul,hGSq,map_sub,map_one,map_mul,hPullA]\n    have hEq : G0=Γ :=\n      AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Measure.L2RealSquareRootUnique.positive_square_roots_unique\n        ν G0 Γ hG0 hΓ (hG0Sq.trans hΓSq.symm)\n    calc\n      G=e.conjStarAlgEquiv G0 := by\n        apply ContinuousLinearMap.ext\n        intro f\n        simp only [G0,LinearIsometryEquiv.conjStarAlgEquiv_apply_apply,\n          LinearIsometryEquiv.symm_symm,e.symm_apply_apply,e.apply_symm_apply]\n      _ = e.conjStarAlgEquiv Γ := congrArg e.conjStarAlgEquiv hEq\n      _ = ΓP := rfl\n",
          "detail": "Exact excerpt from the compiled declaration in its local context; preceding canonical lets and earlier proved facts remain in scope.",
          "lean_source_region": {
            "path": "AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/ProximalBPS/MacroscopicDefectRoot.lean",
            "source_raw_sha256": "1022d344a428efaafd7443c65317c5bde0a2f3ed05161caaac8bf15ae239858a",
            "start_line": 195,
            "end_line": 220,
            "exact_code_raw_sha256": "268d900f99391f9b1a69b9bbf9fa6fbf51c70d17cd30e4d25693e46b1b71803c"
          }
        },
        {
          "title": "Exercise the original-input consumer without certificates",
          "text": "The Test takes the original potential and Hessian/step assumptions, invokes the actual macro theorem, and derives root contractivity from energy and the nonnegativity of ‖Af‖². It does not supply a probability kernel, onto map, defect, root or energy premise.",
          "formula": "0\\le\\|Af\\|^2,\\quad\\|\\Gamma_Pf\\|^2=\\|f\\|^2-\\|Af\\|^2\\ \\Longrightarrow\\ \\|\\Gamma_Pf\\|\\le\\|f\\|.",
          "lean": "  classical\n  let mY : MeasurableSpace (E × E) :=\n    MeasurableSpace.comap Prod.snd (inferInstance : MeasurableSpace E)\n  letI : MeasurableSpace (E × E) := Prod.instMeasurableSpace\n  letI : Fact (mY ≤ (inferInstance : MeasurableSpace (E × E))) :=\n    ⟨measurable_snd.comap_le⟩\n  dsimp only\n  obtain ⟨hμ,hJ,hν,hHP,hPf,S,hS,hSd,hSc,hSf,hSs,e,he,U,hU,hUi,hUs,T,hTs,\n    hT,hA,hAs,hAn,hPB,Γ,hΓ,hΓSq,hΓP,hΓPSq,hGram,hEnergy,hUnique⟩ :=\n    AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.ProximalBPS.MacroscopicDefectRoot.actual_unique_positive_macroscopic_defect_root\n      hα hαβ hV hH hη hβη\n  refine ⟨hμ,hJ,hν,hHP,hPf,S,hS,hSd,hSc,hSf,hSs,e,he,U,hU,hUi,hUs,T,hTs,\n    hT,hA,hAs,hAn,hPB,Γ,hΓ,hΓSq,hΓP,hΓPSq,hGram,?_,hUnique⟩\n  intro f\n  have hf := hEnergy f\n  refine ⟨hf.1,hf.2,?_⟩\n  have hnonneg : 0 ≤ ‖f‖^2 - ‖(e.conjStarAlgEquiv Γ) f‖^2 := by\n    rw [hf.2]\n    simp only [sub_sub_cancel]\n    positivity\n  nlinarith [norm_nonneg ((e.conjStarAlgEquiv Γ) f),norm_nonneg f]\n",
          "detail": "Exact original-input consumer proof, with internally derived measurability Fact and no supplied root/energy premise.",
